    <statement><p>Write an equation of the plane with normal vector <m>\bf{n}</m><m>=\left\lt 6,-5,-7\right&gt;</m> passing through the point <m>\left( -7, 9, -5 \right)</m> in scalar form</p>
<p><fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/><m>= -156</m></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>18x-15y-21z</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\left\lt  6, -5, -7 \right&gt; \cdot \left\lt  x, y, z \right&gt; = \left\lt  6, -5, -7 \right&gt; \cdot \left\lt  -7, 9, -5 \right&gt; = -42 - 45+35=-52</m>



To obtain the scalar form we compute the dot product above



<m>6x-5y-7z=-52</m>



or in the form 



<m>18x-15y-21z=-156</m>


</solution>
